<title>ITALY: Italy's Genoa sees April CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Genoa sees April CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>GENOA, Italy 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Genoa said its April consumer price index stood at 0.0 percent month-on-month and 0.7 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In March, Genoa's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 1.0 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Genoa was one of 11 sample cities publishing inflation data Monday and Tuesday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 2.88 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to March 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0    (0.1)    0.7   (1.0)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.1   (-0.1)   -0.6   (0.2)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.6    (0.1)    2.8   (2.5)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.9    (0.1)    4.3   (4.1)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0    (0.0)    0.6   (0.7)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0    (0.1)    2.2   (2.3)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   -0.1    (0.3)    1.0   (1.4)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.5    (0.2)   -0.5  (-0.2)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.0)    3.9   (4.1)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.1    (0.1)    0.6   (0.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0    (0.2)   -2.3  (-2.4)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
</text>
